<title>JAPAN: Output at big Japan aluminium mills rises in June.</title>
<headline>Output at big Japan aluminium mills rises in June.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Output of fabricated aluminium products at Japan's seven leading mills rose 11.3 percent in June from the same month last year to 145,408 tonnes, according to data submitted by the companies to the Japan Aluminum Federation and released on Thursday. It was the 12th successive monthly rise.</p>
<p>The June data was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    June 97	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	    145,408	 +11.3 pct</p>
<p> Flat-rolled    116,690	 +11.4 pct</p>
<p>   Can stock     41,883	  +7.6 pct</p>
<p> Extrusions	28,718	 +11.0 pct</p>
<p>The seven companies are: Kobe Steel Ltd (includes KAAL, a joint venture with Aluminum Co of America ), Sumitomo Light Metal Industries Ltd, Furukawa Electric Co, Mitsubishi Aluminum Co, Nippon Light Metal Co, Sky Aluminium Co and Showa Aluminum Corp.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
